@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the steps of one agent run on the Host.
' A step is a stage of the run on the Host, not a label on GitHub.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "label changed" as Labeled
Labeled : cumin changed the status label on GitHub

state "prepared" as Prepared
Prepared : the agent work directory, the token,\nthe instructions, the facts, the skills

state "started" as Started
Started : cumin reads the start record

state "running" as Running
Running : do / the agent works

state "ended" as Ended
Ended : cumin checks the result

state "abnormal end" as Abnormal
Abnormal : no result for cumin

state "decided from GitHub" as Decided
Decided : each area decides the next action\nfrom the facts on GitHub

[*] --> Labeled : an area starts an agent\n[the tool checks of the repository pass]
Labeled --> Prepared
Prepared --> Started : cumin starts the CLI\nisolated from the Host user's settings
Started --> Running : [the start record is clean,\nevery skill is there]
Started --> Abnormal : [user-level context,\nor a missing skill]\n/ cumin stops the run
Running --> Ended : the agent returns its result
Running --> Abnormal : [the time limit passed,\nor the process failed]\n/ cumin stops the run and its commands
Ended --> Decided : [the result has the right form]\n/ cumin posts blocked_reason if blocked
Ended --> Abnormal : [the result has the wrong form]
Abnormal --> Decided
Decided --> [*]

@enduml
